            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "All of our other programs have asset tags.  Why are we removing it from Minerva?  Should we go the other direction, of starting to fill out this field?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yang Chen",
                        "email": "yang.chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "Quanta-YangChen"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Patrick,\n\nRegarding Meta Shreyas Rao\u2019s reply about the FCB assert tag field (quoted below):\n\n```\nThe FAN Board is not tied to any L10 hence we do not have any relevant Product Info to tie to.\n\nBoard Info = PCBA Level\nProduct Info = Blade Level\nChassis Info = 30OU Chassis Level\n\nBased on this the FAN Board can only expect Board and Chassis Info. What is the requirement here from LF-BMC?\n```\n\nShould we request adding a new field for this, or can we remove it as this commit proposes?\n\nThanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
